# 10. Database Approach

Codex’s earlier `metadata jsonb` idea still works.

## Keep main entry table

```sql
entries (
  id,
  title,
  area,
  category,
  entry_date,
  next_due_date,
  notes,
  reminder_enabled,
  metadata jsonb,
  created_at,
  updated_at
)
```

## Add one child table: `plan_sessions`

For calendar tracking, avoid storing every session only inside JSON.

```sql
plan_sessions (
  id,
  entry_id,
  session_date,
  session_type,
  title,
  status,
  completed_at,
  score,
  notes,
  metadata jsonb
)
```

Why:

* Easy calendar rendering
* Easy metrics
* Easy filtering by date/status
* Cleaner than deeply nested JSON

